"hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:"
2800,"**
Narrated to us Yusuf ibn Musa, narrated to us Jarir, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, on the authority of Abdullah ibn az-Zubayr (RA), who said:

""From the Sunnah of Hajj is that the Imam prays Zuhr, Asr, Maghrib, Isha, and Fajr at Mina. Then he proceeds to Arafah in the forenoon, and rests wherever he is able until the sun declines. He then addresses the people, after which he prays Zuhr and Asr together. He then stands at Arafah until the sun sets. Then he departs (from Arafah) and prays at al-Muzdalifah, or wherever Allah decrees. He then stands at al-Jam' (Muzdalifah) until it becomes light, after which he departs before the sun rises. When he pelts the Major Jamrah, all restrictions are lifted for him except for women and perfume until he visits the House (Ka'bah)."""
2801,"**
Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Walid, narrated to us Yazid — meaning ibn Harun —, informed us Yahya ibn Sa'id, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, who said: I heard Ibn az-Zubayr say: ""It is from the Sunnah,"" then he mentioned the hadith. And sometimes they differed over a word or a tooth (of the Jamrah). And he said: ""Then what was forbidden to him becomes lawful for him, except women, until he performs Tawaf around the House.""

Abu Bakr said: ""This is the correct view: when he stones the Jamrah, everything becomes lawful for him except women, because 'A'ishah (RA) reported: 'She perfumed the Prophet (ﷺ) before he entered the House (i.e., before performing Tawaf).'"""
